  "question": {
    "text": "A pendulum has an angular amplitude&nbsp;<math><mrow><mi>θ</mi></mrow></math>. The tension in the string at extreme position is T<sub>1</sub> and at the bottom is T<sub>2</sub>. If it is known that T<sub>2</sub> = 2T<sub>1</sub>, then what is the value of&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>cos</mi><mi>θ</mi></math>?"
  },
  "options": [],
  "correct_answer": "0.75",
  "solution": {
